SUMMARY:Belgium: "Loon-datatransfer" tool to replace DmfA
DESCRIPTION:Voluntary from 2027. As part of RSZ's e-gov modernisation\, a n
 ew "loon-datatransfer" (wage data transfer) tool will be available for vol
 untary use and testing from 1 January 2027\, become mandatory from 1 Janua
 ry 2028\, and the DmfA submission itself will be abolished from 1 January 
 2030. RSZ began sending informational letters to employers about the trans
 ition from 28 May 2026.\n\nSource: https://www.unizo.be/berichten/nieuws/i
 nformatiebrieven-rsz\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries
 /belgium.html#be-reporting-upcoming\n\nFor information only\, not legal or
  tax advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/belgium.html#be-reporting-u
 pcoming
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
